{
    "map": {
        "description": "Creates line features that represent sight lines from one or more observer points to features in a  target feature class.",
        "in_observer_points.descr": "The single-point features that represent observer points. Multipoint features are not supported.",
        "in_observer_points.title": "Observer Points",
        "in_target_features.descr": "The target features (points, multipoints, lines, and polygons).",
        "in_target_features.title": "Target Features",
        "join_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The join field is used to match observers to specific targets.</p><ul><li><span title=\"&lt;None&gt;\">No Join Field</span>—No Z values will be assigned to the resulting sight line features.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "join_field.title": "Join Field",
        "observer_height_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The source of the height values for the observer points obtained from its attribute table.</p><p>A default <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Observer Height Field</span> field is selected from among the options listed below by order of priority. If multiple fields exist, and the desired field does not have a higher priority in the default field selection, the desired field will need to be specified.</p><ul><li><span title=\"&lt;None&gt;\">No Height Source</span>—No Z values will be assigned to the resulting sight line features.</li></ul><ul><li> Shape.Z</li><li>Spot</li><li> Z</li><li> Z_Value</li><li>Height</li><li> Elev</li><li> Elevation</li><li> Contour</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "observer_height_field.domain.<None>": "No Height Source",
        "observer_height_field.title": "Observer Height Field",
        "out_line_feature_class.descr": "The output feature class containing the sight lines.",
        "out_line_feature_class.title": "Output",
        "output_the_direction.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies whether to add direction attributes to the output sight lines. Two additional fields will be added and populated to indicate direction: <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">AZIMUTH</span> and <span class=\"esri_fieldname\">VERT_ANGLE</span> (vertical angle).</p><ul><li>Unchecked—No direction attributes will be added to the output sight lines. This is the default.</li><li>Checked—Two additional fields will be added and populated to indicate direction: azimuth and vertical angle.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "output_the_direction.title": "Output The Direction",
        "sample_distance.descr": "<xdoc><p>The distance between samples when the target is either a line or polygon feature class. The <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Sampling Distance</span> units are interpreted in the XY units of the output feature class.</p></xdoc>",
        "sample_distance.title": "Sampling Distance",
        "sampling_method.descr": "<xdoc><p>Specifies how the sampling distance will be used to establish sight lines along the target feature.</p><ul><li><span title=\"2D_DISTANCE\">2D distance</span>—The distance will be evaluated in two-dimensional Cartesian space. This is the default.</li><li><span title=\"3D_DISTANCE\">3D distance</span>—The distance will be evaluated in three-dimensional length.</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "sampling_method.domain.2D_DISTANCE": "2D distance",
        "sampling_method.domain.3D_DISTANCE": "3D distance",
        "sampling_method.title": "Sampling Method",
        "summary": "Creates line features that represent sight lines from one or more observer points to features in a target feature class.",
        "target_height_field.descr": "<xdoc><p>The height field for the target.</p><p>A default <span class=\"esri_uicontrol\">Target Height Field</span> field is selected from among the options listed below by order of priority. If multiple fields exist, and the desired field does not have a higher priority in the default field selection, the desired field will need to be specified.</p><ul><li><span title=\"&lt;None&gt;\">No Height Source</span>—No Z values will be assigned to the resulting sight line features.</li></ul><ul><li> Shape.Z</li><li>Spot</li><li> Z</li><li> Z_Value</li><li>Height</li><li> Elev</li><li> Elevation</li><li> Contour</li></ul></xdoc>",
        "target_height_field.domain.<None>": "No Height Source",
        "target_height_field.title": "Target Height Field",
        "title": "Construct Sight Lines"
    }
}
